; expect-fail: legacy — a handler clause that does NOT resume must discard
; the continuation (abort semantics): the handle's result is 999. The EIR VM
; does this; the legacy interpreter wrongly resumes with the clause value
; (1 + 999 = 1000). Pinned in backend_parity.rs::known_divergences_are_pinned
; too; retire both when the interpreter is fixed or retired.
; expect-fail: wasm — codegen compiles the handler tail-resumptively, so it
; has the same resume-with-clause-value bug as the interpreter (1000).
[effect F [fail [] Int]]
[fn body [] [+ 1 [F.fail]]]
[fn main []
  [println [handle [body] [F.fail] 999]]]
